  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c054", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Every notice must \"specifically refer to the number of this Policy,\" yet the number is given inconsistently across the instrument — CA03607A on the face and in Exhibit A, CA036078 in the Endorsement heading and Exhibit B. A notice bearing one number could be said not to satisfy this requirement.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c055", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Making every Payment Notice and communication \"effective only upon actual receipt by XLCA\" conflicts with the deemed-receipt rules in c040 and c045, which treat notices and documents arriving after 10:00 a.m. as received at 9:00 a.m. the next Business Day. Actual and deemed receipt cannot both govern the same notice.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c056", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The obligations are called \"irrevocable, primary, absolute and unconditional\" in the same breath as being made \"subject to satisfaction of the conditions for making a claim under this Policy.\" The provision contradicts itself on its face about whether the guarantee is conditional.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c057", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"A successful action or proceeding to enforce this Policy\" is undefined and admits of no boundary: partial recovery, settlement, or a claim paid after suit is filed are not addressed. Whether fees follow in those cases cannot be decided from the words.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c058", "issues": [
