  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c070", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Reasonable efforts\" to ensure the funds are applied to the Deficiency Amount, not applied elsewhere, and properly recorded is undefined and measured against no benchmark. What the Securities Administrator must actually do before Owners lose their claim is unstated.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c071", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Here the Securities Administrator purports to assign the Owners' rights and claims, including securities-law claims, whereas Exhibit B (c080) contemplates an assignment executed by the Owner itself or by the Securities Administrator only \"as Owner's attorney-in-fact.\" Which instrument effects the assignment, and on what authority, is unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c072", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Preserving subrogation rights \"in addition to, and not in limitation of\" the assignment leaves those rights unreconciled with c051, which subordinates all subrogation rights acquired on a Policy payment to the Owners' prior payment in full. The saving clause does not say which ranking applies.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c073", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Such action and such instruments as may be reasonably required by XLCA\" is open-ended, with no limit on the burden the Securities Administrator can be put to and no standard for reasonableness. The clause also leaves its own number unresolved (\"[5.] or [6.]\").", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c074", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The appointment of XLCA as \"agent and attorney-in-fact\" for the Owners in \"any legal proceeding in respect of the Insured Obligation\" is unbounded in time and subject matter, and it is made by the Securities Administrator on the Owners' behalf without any stated source of authority. How far the power reaches is undetermined.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c075", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The general grant to \"direct all matters relating to such Insolvency Proceeding\" sits against the enumerated items (a)-(c) that follow, leaving unclear whether the enumeration limits the grant. \"Preference Claim (as defined below)\" also points forward to a definition given only later in the same sentence.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c076", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The paragraph simultaneously says XLCA \"shall be subrogated to\" and that the Securities Administrator \"delegates and assigns\" the Owners' rights \"to the fullest extent permitted by law,\" three different mechanisms with no stated boundary. What rights in fact pass, and against what legal limit, is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.19}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c077", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The Payment Notice refers undefined capitalized terms to the Indenture, yet the terms it actually uses — Deficiency Amount, Insured Note Charge-Off Amount, Avoided Payment — are defined in the Endorsement, and c010 refers Policy terms to the Endorsement rather than the Indenture. The form's referral clause points away from the definitions it depends on.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c078", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c079", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Terms in the assignment take their meanings from \"the Policy including as incorporated by reference therein,\" which chains through c010 to the Endorsement and c016 to the Indenture. Whether \"Owner\" in Exhibit B bears the Endorsement's restricted meaning at c028 depends entirely on that chain.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c080", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The bracketed alternatives \"[paid][or][sought to be recovered from]\" are left unresolved on the face of the form, so it does not say whether the Owner must already have repaid the Avoided Payment before assigning. The assigned subject matter — \"any rights or claims ... against any person\" connected with the Avoided Payment — is also unbounded.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c081", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The Owner warrants the claims free only of liens or encumbrances \"created or incurred by such Owner,\" while c002 conditions XLCA's payment on an assignment of rights and claims \"free of any adverse claim\" from any source. The warranty given is narrower than the condition imposed.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.27}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c082", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"The Owner ... and XLCA shall agree on such other form as is reasonably necessary\" is an agreement to agree, with no fallback if they do not. It also does not say who \"reasonably determines\" the existing form insufficient or how a \"change of law or applicable rules\" is established.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27}
  ]}
]}

